/*! @brief The test module is a testing framework, combined with the assert module, it can easily write various test cases, and can be called as a function

Before writing test cases, it is usually necessary to define a test module to describe the test content.

- describe

describe is the container for all test groups, similar to the concept of test suite, used to hang `it` tests under specific categories, describe can contain multiple it cases or other nested describe subcategories.

```
describe(String name, Function block)
```

Call parameters:
name: String, define module name
block: Function, module initialization code

- it

Represents a single test case, each description should only test a single situation to ensure the reliability of test results.

```
it(String name, Function block)
```

Call parameters:
name: String, define item name
block: Function, test content

- xit & it.skip

Represents skipped test cases.

```
xit(String name, Function block)
```

Call parameters:
name: String, define item name
block: Function, test content

- oit & it.only

Represents running only the current test case, ignoring other test cases, very useful for debugging the current case alone.

```
oit(String name, Function block)
it.only(String name, Function block)
```

Call parameters:
name: String, define item name
block: Function, test content

- todo

Represents the plan for test cases that need further improvement.

```
todo(String name, Function block)
```

Call parameters:
name: String, define item name
block: Function, test content

When writing test cases, usually use the assert assertion module to check the return of functions. Usage is as follows:

```
assert(condition, String message);
```

Among them, the first parameter is the condition to be asserted, the second parameter is the error message.
 */
module test
{
    /*! @brief Define a test item
     @param name Define item name
     @param block Test content
     */
    static Function(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Test framework module, points to this module, can be called as a function */
    static test;

    /*! @brief Test framework module, points to this module, can be called as a function */
    static test new it();

    /*! @brief Test suite module, can be called as a function, see test_suite */
    static test_suite new suite();

    /*! @brief Test suite module, can be called as a function, see test_suite */
    static test_suite new describe();

    /*! @brief Assertion test module, can be called as a function, if the test value is false, report error, error behavior can be set to continue running or throw error */
    static assert;

    /*! @brief Pause test suite definition
     @param name Define module name
     @param block Module initialization code
     */
    static xdescribe(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Independent test suite definition
     @param name Define module name
     @param block Module initialization code
     */
    static odescribe(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Pause test item definition
     @param name Define item name
     @param block Test content
     */
    static xit(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Pause test item definition
     @param name Define item name
     @param block Test content
     */
    static skip(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Independent test item definition
     @param name Define item name
     @param block Test content
     */
    static oit(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Independent test item definition
     @param name Define item name
     @param block Test content
     */
    static only(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Plan item definition
     @param name Define item name
     @param block Test content
     */
    static todo(String name, Function block);

    /*! @brief Define current test module enter event
     @param func Event function
     */
    static before(Function func);

    /*! @brief Define current test module exit event
     @param func Event function
     */
    static after(Function func);

    /*! @brief Define current test module test item enter event
     @param func Event function
     */
    static beforeEach(Function func);

    /*! @brief Define current test module test item exit event
     @param func Event function
     */
    static afterEach(Function func);

    /*! @brief Test that a function must be called a specified number of times
     @param func The function to be tested
     @return Return the wrapped function
     */
    static Function mustCall(Function func);

    /*! @brief Test that a function must not be called
     @param func The function to be tested
     @return Return the wrapped function
     */
    static Function mustNotCall(Function func);

    /*! @brief Test that a function must not be called
     @return Return the wrapped function
    */
    static Function mustNotCall();

    /*! @brief Set and query slow test warning threshold, in ms, default is 75
     */
    static Integer slow;
};